  "warningHeading": "Beta version and liability",
  "warningSection1Title": "1. Beta version",
  "warningSection1Body": "NautiLink is currently offered as a beta version, that is, in a testing phase. Its features (position tracking, sending text messages and e-mails, SOS alerts, logbook) may suffer errors, delays or interruptions, due in particular to mobile network coverage, Internet access, GPS reception, or the state or settings of the phone. Continuity and accuracy of the service are not guaranteed during this phase.",
  "warningSection2Title": "2. NautiLink is not safety equipment",
  "warningSection2Body": "NautiLink is not safety equipment within the meaning of maritime regulations. It replaces neither the mandatory safety equipment (VHF radio, signalling devices, distress beacon, etc.) nor the official alert procedures. In distress, first alert the rescue services on VHF channel 16, 196 or 112. An alert sent by NautiLink, or its failure to be sent, cannot be considered an alert to the rescue services.",
  "warningSection3Title": "3. Skipper's responsibility",
  "warningSection3Body": "The skipper remains solely responsible for handling the vessel, the safety of the people on board, preparing the trip and complying with the regulations in force.",
  "warningSection4Title": "4. Limitation of liability",
  "warningSection4Body": "To the fullest extent permitted by law, the publisher of NautiLink cannot be held liable for indirect damage resulting from a malfunction, interruption or unavailability of the service, or from use of the app that does not comply with its purpose or with this warning.\n\nThis limitation does not apply to personal injury, nor in the event of gross negligence or wilful misconduct by the publisher. It does not deprive users who are consumers of the rights granted to them by law, in particular the French Consumer Code, which cannot be waived.",
